From 154e9806f6dce527143a4d48c91400f35bbc47c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moussa Ouallaf <moussa@husimi.ai>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:31:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Check the input once in pred_param and skip trees that never
 split

pred_param called every base tree with its own input check, which costs
far more than the tree walk itself. When every learner is a scikit-learn
regression tree, pred_param now checks X once (float32, the columns the
trees read, NaN allowed only where every tree allows it) and calls the
trees with check_input=False. A tree whose leaves all hold one value is
replaced by its scalar update. The floating-point operations per
parameter happen in the same order as before, so the output is
bit-identical.

The precomputed plan keeps references to the rounds it was built from
and is rebuilt when they, init_params or learning_rate change. It is not
pickled. max_iter, sparse input and other learners use the loop as
before.

fit and partial_fit warn (NGBoostDegenerateWarning) when every learner
is constant, which happens silently when int(minibatch_frac * n) is below
max(min_samples_split, 2 * min_samples_leaf).

